# Optional machine-specific configuration.
#
# Copy this file to course_config.local, then edit only the paths needed on
# your machine.  Keep shell/Make syntax: NAME=value, with no spaces around "=".

# 1. AFEPack computation: headers, libAFEPack, templates, OpenBLAS, and Boost.
# CXX=/usr/bin/c++
# AFEPACK_PREFIX=/Users/your-name
# OPENBLAS_PREFIX=/opt/local
# BOOST_INCLUDE=/opt/local/libexec/boost/1.81/include
# On macOS this is normally inferred from libAFEPack; override only if needed.
# COURSE_TARGET_ARCH=x86_64
# Usually derived from AFEPACK_PREFIX; uncomment only for a split installation.
# AFEPACK_PATH=/path/to/AFEPack
# AFEPACK_TEMPLATE_PATH=/path/to/triangle:/path/to/twin_triangle

# 2. EasyMesh generation/remeshing: triangulator and AFEPack mesh converter.
# EASYMESH_BIN=/Users/your-name/bin/easymesh
# EASYMESH2MESH_BIN=/Users/your-name/bin/easymesh2mesh

# 3. Optional Python helper/visualization environment.
# Set ENABLE_PYTHON_PLOTS=0 to generate numerical/mesh data without PNG/GIF
# figures in examples where plotting is optional.
# PYTHON_BIN=/path/to/python
# PLOT_PYTHON=/path/to/python
# ENABLE_PYTHON_PLOTS=0

# 4. Raster conversion for C++-generated figures in example 07.
# IMAGE_CONVERT_BIN=/path/to/convert
